message: "If you use proteostasis-sim in your research, please cite both the software archive and the accompanying article."
title: "proteostasis-sim: Multiscale in silico framework for physiological antagonism and competing risks in genetic proteinopathies"
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-11-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lucassbiondini/proteostasis-sim"
url: "https://github.com/lucassbiondini/proteostasis-sim"
orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5753-1000"
abstract: >-
  proteostasis-sim is an open-source, three-scale in silico modeling platform
  coupling nonlinear intracellular proteostasis-bioenergetics (5-ODE/SDE),
  spatial 2D hybrid agent-based and reaction-diffusion PDE tissue remodeling,
  and shared-frailty competing-risks survival analysis (Aalen-Johansen CIF,
  Cox CSH, Fine
